## What is New Nordics AI?

New Nordics AI is a joint initiative of the Nordic and Baltic countries. It is an independent AI center, hosted by national partners that are well established and deeply rooted in their own AI ecosystems. By connecting these ecosystems, the partners create a structure that lets the Nordic and Baltic countries work together where it matters most.

New Nordics AI connects organizations, companies, governments, stakeholders, and people across the region. It organizes collaboration, makes it easier to share knowledge, and encourages cross-regional projects that accelerate the adoption and development of AI in ways that strengthen competitiveness and benefit everyone living in the Nordic and Baltic countries.

{% action href="https://www.newnordics.ai/" label="Visit website" /%}

## Goals

By bringing national AI ecosystems together, New Nordics AI creates a structure for collaboration, generates new knowledge, and makes room for new partnerships and bold ideas that drive the adoption and development of AI.

{% cards %}
{% card title="Faster AI adoption" image="new-nordics-innleiding.png" %}
We strengthen national players' ability to drive AI adoption by scaling proven solutions, removing barriers, and matching real-world challenges with the right expertise and partners.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Stronger regional collaboration and innovation" image="new-nordics-samstarf.png" %}
We start and support cross-border projects and networks, bringing together large companies, authorities, public institutions, and cities to tackle shared business and societal challenges.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Informing national strategy and leadership" image="new-nordics-stefna.png" %}
We give governments the knowledge, foresight, and coordination to strengthen national strategies and amplify the region's voice in shaping Europe's AI agenda.
{% /card %}
{% /cards %}

## Partners

New Nordics AI is built on a partnership of national organizations that are well established and deeply rooted in their AI ecosystems. Their insight, networks, and credibility allow the center to connect governments, companies, institutions, and stakeholders across the region and achieve an impact no single country could achieve alone.

{% cards %}
{% card title="Almannarómur" logo="almannaromur" %}
Iceland's Center for Language Technology and Artificial Intelligence, advancing research, innovation, and the adoption of AI solutions for the Icelandic language and society.
{% /card %}
{% card title="AI Sweden" logo="ai-sweden.png" href="https://www.ai.se/sv" %}
Sweden's national center for applied AI. Its mission is to accelerate the use of AI for the benefit of Swedish society, competitiveness, and everyone living in Sweden.
{% /card %}
{% card title="AI Finland" logo="ai-finland.png" href="https://teknologiateollisuus.fi/en/" %}
Finland's only business network dedicated to AI, bringing together hundreds of members from every sector to drive AI adoption, innovation, and growth.
{% /card %}
{% card title="TEK Norge" logo="tek-norge.png" href="https://teknorge.no/" %}
Norway's leading technology association, driving digital transformation and AI adoption. By engaging politicians and businesses, it aligns AI development with the needs of society and industry.
{% /card %}
{% card title="Digital Dogme" logo="digital-dogme.png" href="https://digitaldogme.dk/" %}
Denmark's platform for collaboration and knowledge on digital transformation and skills development, bringing together stakeholders from every industry to drive digital growth.
{% /card %}
{% /cards %}
